["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A November weekend near Harrison is a real chance at a black tailed buck. Knowing the few rules that bite here keeps it legal and safe.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law. Synopsis edition dated 2 October 2026.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-buck.jpg\" alt=\"Columbian black tailed buck in the Dungeness River, Washington, a doe at left. Red brown coat, dark tail, forked antlers like a mule deer.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Columbian black tailed buck in the Dungeness River, Washington, a doe at left. Red brown coat, dark tail, forked antlers like a mule deer. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Philip Cohen, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Columbian_Black-tailed_Deer_buck.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Harrison Lake: west side and the Chehalis are <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit) 2-19, the east side and Agassiz are 2-18. Mission is 2-8 (90%, page 26 map).</li></ul>","<ul><li>Deer in all three: bucks only, 10 September to 15 December (99%, page 28).</li></ul><div class=\"hm-seasons\" data-region=\"2\" data-mus=\"2-18,2-19,2-8\" data-species=\"mule deer\"><p class=\"hm-law\">Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p><p class=\"muted\">Season table loading...</p></div>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>MUs 2-8, 2-18, 2-19</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General season</td><td>Bucks, Sept 10 to Dec 15</td><td>99%, page 28</td></tr><tr><td>Bow only</td><td>Bucks, Sept 1 to Sept 9</td><td>99%, page 28</td></tr><tr><td>Antlerless (doe, fawn)</td><td>No general season</td><td>99%, page 28</td></tr><tr><td>White tailed deer</td><td>No season in Region 2</td><td>99%, pages 14 and 27</td></tr><tr><td>Region 2 deer limit</td><td>2 a licence year, at most 1 antlerless</td><td>99%, page 27</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset</td><td>99%, page 11, item 38</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","<ul><li>A buck is a deer \"bearing visible bony antlers\" (99%, page 4). These rows say Bucks, not 4 point bucks (99%, page 28).</li></ul><ul><li>In these MUs the antlerless 1 is out of reach: the only rows are bucks (99%, page 28).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the official wording</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Regional Bag Limits, page 27</div><p>\"Deer: Unless otherwise indicated, the bag limit for mule (black-tailed) deer is 2, one of which may be antlerless.\"</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Hours, page 11, item 38</div><p>No hunting game (except migratory birds) from 1 hour after sunset to 1 hour before sunrise.</p></aside><ul><li>The page 28 row reads \"MULE DEER (black tailed)\", MUs \"2-2 to 2-4, 2-6 to 2-8, 2-13 to 2-15, 2-17 to 2-19\", class \"Bucks\", \"Sept 10 to Dec 15\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Province wide, you may take at most 3 deer a licence year (99%, page 14).</li><li>The app works out sunrise and sunset for your spot on the plan and on Home (Tip: check it the night before).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Each hunter: a resident hunting licence ($32.00) plus a deer <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Species licence\">species licence</button> ($15.00) (99%, page 8).</li><li>Kill first, then cancel the licence, then touch the deer (99%, page 11).</li><li>The shooter cancels their own licence, never a partner's <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: licence detail</summary><ul><li>You may hold up to 3 mule deer species licences in a licence year (99%, page 7). A black tailed deer uses the mule deer licence (99%, page 8 fee table: \"Deer (mule, black tailed included, and white tailed)\").</li><li>Fraser Valley Special Area licence: only inside Mission, Maple Ridge, Pitt Meadows and Coquitlam limits in 2-8, and all of 2-4 (99%, Map B10, page 29). Harrison, the Chehalis and the east side are outside it (90%, my reading of Map B10).</li><li>Legal firearm for deer: a centrefire rifle (no .22), among others (99%, page 13).</li><li>Compulsory inspection in Region 2 is for mountain goat and cougar, not deer (99%, page 28). No head or inspection trip for a buck.</li><li>Full detail: <a href=\"#/s/rb-bag-limits/0\">Bag limits and tags</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-doe.jpg\" alt=\"Black tailed doe: the whole top of the tail is dark.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Black tailed doe: the whole top of the tail is dark. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Walter Siegmund (talk), CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odocoileus_hemionus_5432.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-rear.jpg\" alt=\"Mule deer: thin white tail with a black tip.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Mule deer: thin white tail with a black tip. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Buck_(15382465555).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Same species, same licence: the synopsis lists them as \"mule (black-tailed) deer\" (99%, page 27).</li><li>Black tailed: wider tail, dark down the whole top (Tip).</li><li>Antlers fork like a mule deer's (99%, page 4).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ID detail</summary><ul><li>Black tailed deer are the coast deer, the ones around Mission and Harrison (85%, BC Ministry of Environment).</li><li>A white tail has a wide brown tail that flags up white <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. There is no white tailed deer season in Region 2, and some live near Hope at Herrling Island (99%, page 27). Be sure before you shoot.</li><li>More photos: <a href=\"#/s/gallery-deer/0\">Deer gallery</a>.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>November into early December is the black tailed rut <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Bucks move more by day (Tip).</li><li>Cutblock edges, old roads, salal and alder (90%, Region 2 Rule Book strategy).</li><li>Snow over about 30 cm: deer move under old timber crowns, or to low south facing slopes (80 to 85%, Wet forests lesson).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where detail</summary><ul><li>Coast black tailed deer use logged ground often in spring and summer (80%, BC Ministry of Environment).</li><li>Winter foods: Douglas fir, western redcedar, red huckleberry, salal, deer fern and tree lichens <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Timber deer: still hunt slowly with short shots, not long glassing (Tip).</li><li>Spots: open the <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a>, filter deer, and use the Good for 2 and Good solo tags (Tip). Every spot is a candidate: scout it first.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 622\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Zones of fire, seen from above. Walking side by side: hunters A and B walk in sight of each other and in line. Each shoots only in an arc of about 45 degrees straight ahead of them; the wedge between them is NO SHOT. Small boat: two hunters sit back to back, the bow shooter covers the arc off the bow and the stern shooter the arc off the stern; never shoot toward your partner. Sit to shoot, never swing past your partner, motor off and anchored. The width of the boat arcs is an illustration only: no source gives an angle for a boat.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"622\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Walking side by side</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"236\" fill=\"#e9eddf\"/>\n<path d=\"M13 236 l2 -6 M17 236 l0 -7 M21 236 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#b9c29a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M390 159 l2 -6 M394 159 l0 -7 M398 159 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#b9c29a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Your zone of fire|The only slice of ground where you may shoot: about 45 degrees straight ahead. Every shot also needs a safe backstop. Sky is never one.\"><path d=\"M128 232 L63.7 76.8 A168 168 0 0 1 192.3 76.8z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"Partner zone|B shoots only in their own slice. Never swing the muzzle outside your zone, even tracking a running deer.\"><path d=\"M272 232 L207.7 76.8 A168 168 0 0 1 336.3 76.8z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"No shot zone|The middle and behind are no shot zones. A deer runs into the gap: hold fire.\"><path d=\"M128.0 232.0 L192.3 76.8 L207.7 76.8 L272.0 232.0z\" fill=\"#f6cfc0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO SHOT</text></g>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A shoots</text>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">here only</text>\n<text x=\"272\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B shoots</text>\n<text x=\"272\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">here only</text>\n<path d=\"M107.3 182.1 A54 54 0 0 1 148.7 182.1\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45°</text>\n<g data-tip=\"In sight, in line|Walk side by side, always in sight. Lose sight of each other: muzzles up or down, no shooting, call out.\"><line x1=\"144\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"256\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(128 232) rotate(0) scale(1.05)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(272 232) rotate(0) scale(1.05)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in sight, in line</text></g>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Each arc about 45 degrees, straight ahead</text>\n<line x1=\"14\" y1=\"318\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"318\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Small boat, back to back</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"358\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#dbe7ef\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 378 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M330 382 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M10 532 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M350 536 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M100 374 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M186 538 q8 -4 16 0 t16 0\" stroke=\"#b6cddd\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Back to back|Two hunters sit back to back: the bow shooter faces forward, the stern shooter faces back. Shoot sitting, never stand. Arc width here is an illustration only: no source gives a boat angle.\"><path d=\"M168 446 L29.4 503.4 A150 150 0 0 1 29.4 388.6z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M236 446 L374.6 388.6 A150 150 0 0 1 374.6 503.4z\" fill=\"#a9b98a\" stroke=\"#6f7f52\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M112 424 H282 C312 424 334 438 344 446 C334 454 312 468 282 468 H112 C104 468 100 462 100 446 C100 430 104 424 112 424z\" fill=\"#c9b48a\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"106\" y=\"437\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55524c\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(168 446) rotate(270) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(236 446) rotate(90) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M3 -6 L4 -30\" stroke=\"#3b2a1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#7a2f06\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M-5 -4 Q0 -11 5 -4z\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/></g>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stern arc</text>\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bow arc</text>\n<rect x=\"37.8\" y=\"508.0\" width=\"112.2\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"93.887\" y=\"527\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stern shooter</text>\n<line x1=\"164\" y1=\"456\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"508\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"456\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"252.0\" y=\"508.0\" width=\"105.8\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"304.903\" y=\"527\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bow shooter</text>\n<line x1=\"240\" y1=\"456\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"508\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"456\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<g data-tip=\"Never toward your partner|Never shoot toward your partner. Only one person moves at a time. Unload before anyone changes seats.\"><rect x=\"157.4\" y=\"362.0\" width=\"85.3\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"381\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c92a2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO SHOT</text>\n<line x1=\"202\" y1=\"438\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"389\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"438\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#c92a2a\"/></g>\n<g data-tip=\"Loaded in a boat|From 1 October 2026, a BC hunting exemption allows a loaded firearm in a boat with no motor, or while the motor is not moving the boat.\"><text x=\"200\" y=\"570\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sit to shoot. Never swing past</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"591\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">your partner. Motor off, anchored.</text></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"614\" font-size=\"14\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#55524c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Boat arcs: illustration only, no sourced angle</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pair: one sits at a crossing or glasses, the other walks the edge slowly toward the stander, wind at the walker's back (Tip).</li><li>Pair: agree zones of fire, a meeting point and a clock time (Tip).</li><li>Solo: pick a short pack out, 1 km or less and 100 m climb or less (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pair and solo detail</summary><ul><li>Pushes are on foot only (99%, page 11, item 25).</li><li>BC has no blaze orange law. Wear it anyway with a partner (95% for the law, Tip for the advice).</li><li>Solo: leave a trip plan with someone at home, with your truck, the road and the time you will be out (75%, AdventureSmart).</li><li>Solo: a buck on the ground alone is a lot of work. Quarter it if the pack out is long (Tip).</li><li>Full lessons: <a href=\"#/s/hunting-partner/0\">Hunting with a partner</a>, <a href=\"#/s/packing-out/0\">Packing out</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>The radio call in 4 parts</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"First say the road name as it is written on the entry sign.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Road name</text>\n<rect x=\"90.8\" y=\"145.6\" width=\"38.400000000000006\" height=\"64.0\" rx=\"6.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"119.6\" y1=\"145.6\" x2=\"119.6\" y2=\"113.6\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4.800000000000001\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"98.8\" y=\"155.2\" width=\"22.400000000000002\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"190.4\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"90\" width=\"210\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"275\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Road name</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"158\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">as on the sign</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"285.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Say the name on the sign.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Road name, as on the sign.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Then the kilometre sign you are at.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Kilometre</text>\n<rect x=\"90.8\" y=\"145.6\" width=\"38.400000000000006\" height=\"64.0\" rx=\"6.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"119.6\" y1=\"145.6\" x2=\"119.6\" y2=\"113.6\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4.800000000000001\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"98.8\" y=\"155.2\" width=\"22.400000000000002\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"190.4\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"90\" width=\"210\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"275\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Kilometre</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"158\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the sign you just passed</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"285.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Say the kilometre you are at.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> The kilometre you are at.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Then up if the numbers are climbing, down if they are dropping.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Up or down</text>\n<rect x=\"90.8\" y=\"145.6\" width=\"38.400000000000006\" height=\"64.0\" rx=\"6.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"119.6\" y1=\"145.6\" x2=\"119.6\" y2=\"113.6\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4.800000000000001\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"98.8\" y=\"155.2\" width=\"22.400000000000002\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"190.4\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"90\" width=\"210\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"275\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Up or Down</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"158\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">numbers rising = up</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"285.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Up: numbers rising. Down: falling.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Up or down.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Add vehicle type or anything else the sign asks for, at the posted kilometre signs.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"39\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">What the sign asks</text>\n<rect x=\"90.8\" y=\"145.6\" width=\"38.400000000000006\" height=\"64.0\" rx=\"6.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"119.6\" y1=\"145.6\" x2=\"119.6\" y2=\"113.6\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4.800000000000001\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"98.8\" y=\"155.2\" width=\"22.400000000000002\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"190.4\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"90\" width=\"210\" height=\"90\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"275\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Vehicle type</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"158\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">if the sign asks</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"285.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Call at every posted kilometre sign.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Anything else the sign asks.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Sts'ailes (West) <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"FSR\">FSR</button> (Forest Service Road), locally Harrison West, is run by the Chilliwack district (95%, BC government).</li></ul><ul><li>Use the radio channel on the road entry sign. The app gives no channel numbers <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Active hauling: the district page posts no hauling schedule. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at the road sign or the district office.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: road notices and no shooting bands</summary><ul><li>Chilliwack district notices, page last updated 21 October 2026 (95%, BC government road safety page): Harrison East FSR, rockfall hazard \"No Stopping\" signs near 13 km, caution at 2, 13, 16.1 and 21.3 to 22.8 km, no access past 55 km through to the Kookipi FSR. Francis Lake FSR narrow at about 1.3 km (12 May 2026). Mystery 5500 FSR no access past 0 km, washout at 2.0 km. Hemlock Valley FSR no access at 0 km, four washed out culverts. Fleetwood FSR no vehicle access past 5.0 km. The district map also flags a post wildfire rockfall area on the Mystery FSR: do not stop. Read the page before you go: <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/natural-resource-use/resource-roads/local-road-safety-information/chilliwack-natural-resource-district-district-road-safety-information\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chilliwack road safety</a>.</li><li>Sts'ailes (West) FSR (Harrison West) and the Chehalis FSR: no notice posted on the district page or map on 23 October 2026 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. No notice is not a promise the road is open.</li><li>Unless lawfully hunting or trapping, no firearm discharge within 400 m of select FVRD (Fraser Valley Regional District) roads, the Chehalis area on Map B33, and Crown land along the Francis Lake, Weaver Lake and Sts'ailes (West) FSRs (99%, page 27; Closed Areas Regulation Schedule 5.1). Hunting is allowed; target shooting is not (90%, my reading).</li><li>Map B29 Elbow Lake: No Shooting Area 800 m either side of the Chehalis road for 2.4 km north of Elbow Lake (99%, page 31).</li><li>Map B32 Hemlock Valley: No Shooting Area 50 m, then 150 m, either side of the Hemlock Valley road (99%, page 31).</li><li>Harrison Mills and Nicomen lowland: no rifles, and shot only on much of it (99%, Closed Areas Regulation Schedules 9 and 11; 85% my reading of the boundary). Hunt deer up in the hills, not on the flats.</li><li>Highway 7 and Highway 1: shot only within 150 m (99%, Schedule 9 s. 1). Never shoot on or across a road allowance (99%, page 10).</li><li>No hunting or shooting within 100 m of a house, farm building, school or regional district park (99%, page 10 and 9).</li><li>Sasquatch and Kilby provincial parks: closed to hunting. Neither is on Schedule B of the Park, Conservancy and Recreation Area Regulation, so no firearm outside a vehicle and no shooting there (99%, sections 28 and 29).</li><li>Harrison Hot Springs village: no firearm discharge anywhere inside the village, and no shot that goes into, over or through it (99%, Discharge of Firearms Bylaw No. 1207, 2024, section 3). There is no hunting exception.</li><li>The Hunt Map: turn on No shooting / no hunting, and read \"Still check yourself\" in Can I hunt here now?</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule: on a logging road, the truck always wins. Pull over early and let it by.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Shooting a doe because \"the limit is 2, one antlerless\". There is no antlerless season in 2-8, 2-18 or 2-19.</li><li>Taking a rifle onto the Harrison Mills flats. That lowland bans rifles.</li><li>Driving a closed or washed out FSR because a map shows it open.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>The night before: read the Chilliwack road notices, check sunrise for your spot, cancel tags in your head (kill, cancel, touch), and tell someone at home where you will be.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Synopsis 2026 to 2028, 2 October 2026 edition, pages 4, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 26 to 31. Checked 2026-10-17 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and link</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028 (PDF)</a>, edition dated 2 October 2026, read directly 2026-10-17 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/76_84_01\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Closed Areas Regulation, B.C. Reg. 76/84</a>, Schedules 5.1, 9 and 11, consolidation current to 13 October 2026, read directly 2026-10-17 (99%; boundaries my reading, 85%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/natural-resource-use/resource-roads/local-road-safety-information/chilliwack-natural-resource-district-district-road-safety-information\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Chilliwack Natural Resource District road safety information</a>, last updated 21 October 2026, read directly 2026-10-23, with the district's FSR safety map layer <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/180_90_03\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Park, Conservancy and Recreation Area Regulation, Schedule B</a>, current to 20 October 2026, and <a href=\"https://www.harrisonhotsprings.ca/sites/default/files/2024-06/Bylaw-1207---Discharge-of-Firearms.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Harrison Hot Springs Discharge of Firearms Bylaw No. 1207</a>, adopted 27 May 2024, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/natural-resource-use/resource-roads/local-road-safety-information/sea-to-sky-natural-resource-district-road-safety-information/road-conditions-in-sea-to-sky-district\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sea to Sky district road conditions</a>: \"Sts'ailes (West) FSR (locally known as Harrison West)\", managed by the Chilliwack district, read 2026-10-17 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>App lessons used for ID, habitat and tactics: <a href=\"#/s/mule-deer/0\">Mule deer</a>, <a href=\"#/s/gallery-deer/0\">Deer gallery</a>, <a href=\"#/s/wet-forest-country/0\">Wet forests</a>, <a href=\"#/s/the-rut/0\">The rut</a>, <a href=\"#/s/hunting-partner/0\">Hunting with a partner</a>, <a href=\"#/s/fsr-vehicles-radio/0\">Vehicles, Forest Service Roads and radio use</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/0\">Rule Book: Region 2</a>.</li></ul></details>"]